e harbor, bobbing gently like sleeping seals. \n\nHe found a rusty hinge in the toolbox. It was a right hinge, but it would do. He hammered it into place, the sound echoing in the hushed atmosphere. He then found a log, old and dry, and filled them out to make himself a piece with that I message. That\u2019s when he grabbed the hook. \n\nAs evening descended, he stepped into the boat, a vessel filled with memories and regrets. As he tossed the fog off its was, the salty air danced around his feet.\n\nHe adjusted its sail. Was it windy enough?\n\nSuddenly, a flicker of light cut through the gloom. A steady beam, piercing the darkness and illuminating the path ahead. A reassurance, a guide, a promise of safe passage through the storm. He allowed himself to be guided.\n\n\n\nHe was born on the water. Spent his first year looking at the horizon. He reached the town. This was not a port because he took a little silent. The area was silent and there was a small shack. Then he realized something was quiet because there were no seagulls. And there' was the smell of bleach. *They* were gone.  kind of the view changed. \n\n\n\nHe felt the sand between his toes. He thanked the ghost of his dad.",
